  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "In the sequence \\[ \\ldots,a,b,c,d,0,1,1,2,3,5,8,\\ldots \\] each term is the sum of the two terms to its left. Find \\(a.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-3\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(3\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "For three consecutive terms \\(u,v,w\\), the given rule says \\(u+v=w\\), so \\(u=w-v\\). This lets us recover earlier terms from the known neighboring terms \\(0\\) and \\(1\\):\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nd+0=1&\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad d=1,\\\\\nc+d=0&\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad c=0-1=-1,\\\\\nb+c=d&\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad b=1-(-1)=2,\\\\\na+b=c&\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad a=-1-2=-3.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nEach step uniquely determines the next missing term to the left. Thus \\(\\boxed{a=-3}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
